{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794312923065,"sessionID":"ses_e3ab6a190ffeefD3lk4C1wi2O7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_OZJOcMhhOMOrXO1NijJjWgor","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Trim URL shortener\n2: \n3: ## Run contract\n4: \n5: - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n6: - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n7: - The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n8: - Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n9: \n10: ## Layout\n11: \n12: - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n13: - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n14: \n15: Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and hashes and is installed directly. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n16: \n17: ## Container\n18: \n19: ```sh\n20: docker build -t trim .\n21: docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" -e ADMIN_PASSWORD trim\n22: ```\n23: \n24: Set `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your shell before starting the container to enable the reserved `admin` account. If it is unset or empty, admin sign-in is disabled. There is no default admin password. Changing or removing it invalidates existing admin sessions.\n25: \n26: ## Local development\n27: \n28: From the workspace root:\n29: \n30: ```sh\n31: python3 -m venv .venv\n32: . .venv/bin/activate\n33: pip install -r backend/requirements.lock\n34: pip install -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\n35: gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n36: ```\n37: \n38: In a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n39: \n40: ```sh\n41: npm ci\n42: npm run dev\n43: ```\n44: \n45: Vite proxies `/api` and `/r` to Flask. `npm run build` creates the production frontend, which Flask serves directly on port 8000. SQLite is stored at `data/shortlinks.sqlite3` relative to the server's working directory. Back up the data directory while the server is stopped to include SQLite's WAL files safely.\n46: \n47: ## Verification\n48: \n49: ```sh\n50: python3 -m unittest discover -s backend -p 'test_*.py' -v\n51: ruff check backend\n52: npm --prefix frontend run lint\n53: npm --prefix frontend run typecheck\n54: npm --prefix frontend run build\n55: ```\n56: \n57: Browser tests cover registration, sign-in, validation, copying, paging, deletion, and moderation at desktop and mobile sizes:\n58: \n59: ```sh\n60: npm --prefix frontend exec -- playwright install chromium\n61: npm --prefix frontend run test:e2e\n62: ```\n63: \n64: The browser test server uses a temporary SQLite database, never your persistent data. Set `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` to use an already installed Chromium binary instead of downloading one.\n65: \n66: ## API\n67: \n68: Register with `POST /api/auth/register` and sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`, supplying JSON `username` and `password`. Use the returned token as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on authenticated requests. Tokens expire after 30 days, are stored hashed in SQLite, and survive restarts. `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token; `GET /api/auth/me` returns the signed-in user.\n69: \n70: Create a link with `POST /api/links` and JSON `{\"original_url\": \"https://example.com\"}`. Link objects contain `id`, `original_url`, `short_code`, `short_url` (a relative `/r/<code>` path), `click_count`, `created_at` (UTC ISO 8601), `owner` (username), and `is_active`.\n71: \n72: `GET /api/links` and `GET /api/links/{id}` are public. `DELETE /api/links/{id}` is restricted to the owner. `GET /api/admin/links` includes disabled links; `POST /api/admin/links/{id}/toggle` switches their active state. Disabled links return 404 on public detail, delete, and redirect endpoints.\n73: \n74: List responses are `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n, \"page\": n, \"page_size\": n}`. Paging defaults to page 1 with 10 items, and supports 1–100 items per page. Lists sort newest first and accept an optional `q` search. `GET /api/links/mine` lists the signed-in user's active links. `GET /api/stats` returns community-wide active-link counts, clicks, and links created today (UTC). Validation errors return JSON `{\"error\": \"message\"}`.\n\n(End of file - total 74 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Trim URL shortener\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and hashes and is installed directly. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n## Container\n\n```sh\ndocker build -t trim .","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# Trim URL shortener\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and hashes and is installed directly. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n## Container\n\n```sh\ndocker build -t trim .\ndocker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" -e ADMIN_PASSWORD trim\n```\n\nSet `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your shell before starting the container to enable the reserved `admin` account. If it is unset or empty, admin sign-in is disabled. There is no default admin password. Changing or removing it invalidates existing admin sessions.\n\n## Local development\n\nFrom the workspace root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -m venv .venv\n. .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r backend/requirements.lock\npip install -r backend/requirements-dev.txt\ngunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n```\n\nIn a second terminal, from `frontend/`:\n\n```sh\nnpm ci\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nVite proxies `/api` and `/r` to Flask. `npm run build` creates the production frontend, which Flask serves directly on port 8000. SQLite is stored at `data/shortlinks.sqlite3` relative to the server's working directory. Back up the data directory while the server is stopped to include SQLite's WAL files safely.\n\n## Verification\n\n```sh\npython3 -m unittest discover -s backend -p 'test_*.py' -v\nruff check backend\nnpm --prefix frontend run lint\nnpm --prefix frontend run typecheck\nnpm --prefix frontend run build\n```\n\nBrowser tests cover registration, sign-in, validation, copying, paging, deletion, and moderation at desktop and mobile sizes:\n\n```sh\nnpm --prefix frontend exec -- playwright install chromium\nnpm --prefix frontend run test:e2e\n```\n\nThe browser test server uses a temporary SQLite database, never your persistent data. Set `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH` to use an already installed Chromium binary instead of downloading one.\n\n## API\n\nRegister with `POST /api/auth/register` and sign in with `POST /api/auth/login`, supplying JSON `username` and `password`. Use the returned token as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on authenticated requests. Tokens expire after 30 days, are stored hashed in SQLite, and survive restarts. `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token; `GET /api/auth/me` returns the signed-in user.\n\nCreate a link with `POST /api/links` and JSON `{\"original_url\": \"https://example.com\"}`. Link objects contain `id`, `original_url`, `short_code`, `short_url` (a relative `/r/<code>` path), `click_count`, `created_at` (UTC ISO 8601), `owner` (username), and `is_active`.\n\n`GET /api/links` and `GET /api/links/{id}` are public. `DELETE /api/links/{id}` is restricted to the owner. `GET /api/admin/links` includes disabled links; `POST /api/admin/links/{id}/toggle` switches their active state. Disabled links return 404 on public detail, delete, and redirect endpoints.\n\nList responses are `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n, \"page\": n, \"page_size\": n}`. Paging defaults to page 1 with 10 items, and supports 1–100 items per page. Lists sort newest first and accept an optional `q` search. `GET /api/links/mine` lists the signed-in user's active links. `GET /api/stats` returns community-wide active-link counts, clicks, and links created today (UTC). Validation errors return JSON `{\"error\": \"message\"}`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":74,"totalLines":74,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794312923026,"end":1794312923050}},"id":"prt_1c562678d001HOV5eWcgIGV4eC","sessionID":"ses_e3ab6a190ffeefD3lk4C1wi2O7","messageID":"msg_1c5624f6d001jVo2KKOucp2WuF"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794312923065,"sessionID":"ses_e3ab6a190ffeefD3lk4C1wi2O7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_oHIjB0NTzli7teUmrPyMvUP0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/playwright.config.ts"},"output":"<path>/workspace/frontend/playwright.config.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import { defineConfig } from \"@playwright/test\";\n2: \n3: export default defineConfig({\n4:   testDir: \"./tests\",\n5:   fullyParallel: false,\n6:   workers: 1,\n7:   use: {\n8:     baseURL: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001\",\n9:     screenshot: \"only-on-failure\",\n10:     trace: \"retain-on-failure\",\n11:     launchOptions: { executablePath: process.env.PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH },\n12:   },\n13:   projects: [\n14:     { name: \"desktop\", use: { viewport: { width: 1440, height: 1080 } } },\n15:     { name: \"mobile\", use: { viewport: { width: 390, height: 844 }, isMobile: true, hasTouch: true } },\n16:   ],\n17:   webServer: {\n18:     command: \"python3 tests/server.py\",\n19:     url: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/health\",\n20:     reuseExistingServer: false,\n21:     timeout: 30000,\n22:   },\n23: });\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import { defineConfig } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: \"./tests\",\n  fullyParallel: false,\n  workers: 1,\n  use: {\n    baseURL: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001\",\n    screenshot: \"only-on-failure\",\n    trace: \"retain-on-failure\",\n    launchOptions: { executablePath: process.env.PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH },\n  },\n  projects: [\n    { name: \"desktop\", use: { viewport: { width: 1440, height: 1080 } } },\n    { name: \"mobile\", use: { viewport: { width: 390, height: 844 }, isMobile: true, hasTouch: true } },\n  ],\n  webServer: {\n    command: \"python3 tests/server.py\",\n    url: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/health\",\n    reuseExistingServer: false,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],